# Reviewed allowlist — guards whose subject IS private-address space.
# Each rule names a file and the exact pattern it must be allowed to contain.
# No estate host, IP or credential is allowlisted; every literal below is a
# generic placeholder (`100.64.0.x`, `*.internal` fixture names).

src/config.py:\.internal                          # docstring examples of proxy targets, not estate hosts
src/services/curl_cffi_scraper.py:\.internal      # docstring describes the block rule
src/services/scraper_manager.py:\.internal        # comment describing the SSRF guard
src/services/url_guard.py:\.internal              # the blocklist suffix constant and its docstrings
src/services/url_guard.py:100\.64\.               # docstring documents the RFC 6598 range
tests/test_curl_cffi_scraper.py:\.internal        # fixture host `foo.internal`, not an estate host
tests/test_url_guard.py:\.internal                # fixtures use reserved-style `.internal` names
tests/test_url_guard.py:100\.64\.                 # RFC 6598 SSRF subjects
